    "lawSection": "Local Government, Office of",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5655\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm certain actions taken\nby the town of Schodack, in the county of Rensselaer, with respect to\ncertain bond anticipation notes\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe legislation is to provide legislative relief by validating and\nratifying the town's actions with respect to the Subject BAN\nnotwithstanding the Town of Schodack not making an additional\nprincipal payment in 2006 or 2007.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one- On September 16, 2005, the Town of Schodack (the \"Town\")\nadopted two bond resolutions (respectively, the \"$160,000 Resolution\"\nand the \"$268,000 Resolution,\" and, collectively, the \"Resolutions\")\nin anticipation of financing the costs of two related purposes that\nwould both eventually be within the scope of a project (a \"Project\")\nfor which proceeds from the New York State Environmental Facilities\nCorporation (\"EFC\") would be used. On October 14, 2005, pursuant to\nthe Resolutions, the Town issued a bond anticipation note in the\namount of $428,000 (the \"Subject BAN\"), the proceeds of which were\nused for costs associated with the Project.\n\nOn October 13, 2006, the Town renewed the Subject BAN in the reduced\namount of $419,960, reflecting a payment of principal of $8,040 from\nsources other than proceeds of the Subject BAN renewal. All of the\n$8,040 was allocated to the part of the BAN authorized by the $268,000\nResolution, leaving a balance under that part of the BAN of$259,960.\n\nIn September 2006, the Town had issued a note to EFC (the \"EFC Note\")\nin the amount of $1,098,647 in anticipation of obtaining permanent\nfinancing from EFC (the \"Permanent EFC Financing\"). In September 2007,\nproceeds from the EFC Note in the amount of $419,960 were used to\nrefund the Subject BAN. Neither at that time nor at any time during\n2006 or 2007 (other than as described above) was an additional payment\nof principal made either towards the Subject BAN, as renewed, or\ntowards the EFC Note.  In September 2008, the Town paid, from funds\nnot borrowed, $38,000 toward the outstanding principal of the EFC\nNote, then $1,098,647.\n\nThe Town violated the provisions of subdivisions b-1 and d of Section\n21.00 of the Local Finance Law and subdivision b of the Section 23.00\nof the Local Finance Law by not making an additional principal payment\ntowards the Subject BAN in 2006 or 2007.\n\nSection two-The 2006 BAN and the EFC Note are validated and ratified.\n\nSection three- states bonds, bond anticipation notes issued under\nauthority of the bond resolutions shall be issued in accordance with\nthe provisions of the local finance law.\n\nSection four- contains the separability clause.\n\nSection five- effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Town violated the provisions of subdivisions b-l and d of Section\n21.00 of the Local Finance Law and subdivision b of the Section 23.00\nof the Local Finance Law by not making an additional principal payment\ntowards the Subject BAN in 2006 or 2007. The purpose of the\nLegislation is to provide legislative relief by validating and\nratifying the Town's actions with respect to the Subject BAN\n\nnotwithstanding the Town's not making such an additional principal\npayment in 2006 or 2007.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
